1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,270
Last time, clear glass let most light pass through: transparent.

2
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:08,330
Frosted glass let only some light pass through: translucent.

3
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:10,420
Now, the white wooden door!

4
00:00:13,674 --> 00:00:14,904
Lock in first.

5
00:00:15,154 --> 00:00:17,494
A little moth is hiding in this video.

6
00:00:17,784 --> 00:00:18,984
Can you spot it?

7
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:20,711
Today you'll learn:

8
00:00:20,913 --> 00:00:21,633
Opaque.

9
00:00:22,024 --> 00:00:23,524
What transparency is.

10
00:00:23,727 --> 00:00:25,847
Transparent, translucent, opaque.

11
00:00:27,533 --> 00:00:28,413
Round one.

12
00:00:28,723 --> 00:00:30,713
A wooden door, painted white.

13
00:00:30,983 --> 00:00:32,503
The torch shines on it.

14
00:00:32,783 --> 00:00:34,493
How much light will pass through?

15
00:00:34,763 --> 00:00:35,763
One, most.

16
00:00:36,053 --> 00:00:37,253
Two, only some.

17
00:00:37,543 --> 00:00:38,453
Three, none.

18
00:00:38,753 --> 00:00:40,233
Show me with your fingers.

19
00:00:45,706 --> 00:00:46,686
Locked in!

20
00:00:46,814 --> 00:00:47,594
Two!

21
00:00:47,664 --> 00:00:49,704
It is white, and white is bright!

22
00:00:49,756 --> 00:00:50,496
Three!

23
00:00:50,606 --> 00:00:53,136
Nobody found my robot behind that door!

24
00:00:53,186 --> 00:00:53,726
Three.

25
00:00:55,048 --> 00:00:56,198
Look closer.

26
00:00:56,798 --> 00:00:57,728
Torch on.

27
00:00:58,318 --> 00:01:00,238
The front of the door is bright.

28
00:01:01,749 --> 00:01:03,239
Now look behind it.

29
00:01:03,819 --> 00:01:05,239
No bright spot.

30
00:01:05,829 --> 00:01:06,799
No glow.

31
00:01:07,419 --> 00:01:08,939
No light passed through.

32
00:01:10,852 --> 00:01:12,042
And the robot?

33
00:01:12,602 --> 00:01:14,342
It is still behind the door.

34
00:01:14,932 --> 00:01:16,262
We cannot see it.

35
00:01:20,337 --> 00:01:21,697
The answer is three.

36
00:01:21,997 --> 00:01:22,737
None!

37
00:01:22,787 --> 00:01:23,387
Oh!

38
00:01:23,647 --> 00:01:25,347
White is only its colour!

39
00:01:25,398 --> 00:01:26,488
Three fingers?

40
00:01:26,758 --> 00:01:27,968
One finger up!

41
00:01:28,468 --> 00:01:29,718
Say it with me!

42
00:01:30,428 --> 00:01:33,518
Some materials do not allow any light to pass through them.

43
00:01:34,228 --> 00:01:36,138
These materials are opaque.

44
00:01:40,039 --> 00:01:41,129
A rubber mat.

45
00:01:41,409 --> 00:01:42,499
A metal tray.

46
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:45,059
Torch on: no light passes through.

47
00:01:45,262 --> 00:01:48,142
Rubber, wood and metal are opaque materials.

48
00:01:48,412 --> 00:01:51,762
You cannot see objects placed behind opaque materials.

49
00:01:53,162 --> 00:01:54,312
Three sheets.

50
00:01:54,892 --> 00:01:56,202
The same torch.

51
00:01:56,822 --> 00:01:57,843
Look closer.

52
00:01:57,863 --> 00:01:58,923
Most light.

53
00:01:59,503 --> 00:02:00,793
Only some light.

54
00:02:01,373 --> 00:02:02,343
No light.

55
00:02:02,363 --> 00:02:04,133
How much light can pass through?

56
00:02:04,713 --> 00:02:05,933
That has a name.

57
00:02:09,534 --> 00:02:10,694
Say it with me!

58
00:02:11,402 --> 00:02:15,092
The transparency of a material refers to how much light can pass

59
00:02:15,112 --> 00:02:15,892
through it.

60
00:02:21,216 --> 00:02:22,196
Be the light!

61
00:02:22,466 --> 00:02:23,456
Shrink down.

62
00:02:23,736 --> 00:02:24,666
Quietly.

63
00:02:26,954 --> 00:02:29,734
You are light from a lamp, in a flat at night.

64
00:02:30,391 --> 00:02:31,521
A wooden door.

65
00:02:32,341 --> 00:02:33,291
You stop.

66
00:02:34,121 --> 00:02:35,621
You cannot pass through.

67
00:02:36,345 --> 00:02:37,775
A frosted window.

68
00:02:38,545 --> 00:02:40,185
Only some of you pass through.

69
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:42,380
A clear glass window.

70
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,910
Most of you pass through, out into the night!

71
00:02:48,623 --> 00:02:49,613
My notes!

72
00:02:49,893 --> 00:02:52,073
One: a metal tray is opaque.

73
00:02:52,173 --> 00:02:55,333
Two: this box is plastic, so it is transparent.

74
00:02:55,573 --> 00:02:58,253
Three: frosted glass is translucent.

75
00:02:58,527 --> 00:02:59,427
Showdown!

76
00:02:59,737 --> 00:03:00,867
Double points.

77
00:03:01,137 --> 00:03:02,757
One line has a mistake.

78
00:03:03,047 --> 00:03:04,807
Line one, two, or three?

79
00:03:05,107 --> 00:03:06,577
Show me with your fingers.

80
00:03:13,052 --> 00:03:14,032
Locked in!

81
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:14,950
Two!

82
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:17,320
I cannot see clearly into that box.

83
00:03:17,371 --> 00:03:18,011
Two!

84
00:03:18,151 --> 00:03:19,921
My lunch looks blurry in there!

85
00:03:19,974 --> 00:03:20,634
Oops!

86
00:03:21,636 --> 00:03:22,866
Let's test it.

87
00:03:23,466 --> 00:03:24,606
Look closer.

88
00:03:25,619 --> 00:03:27,299
A clear plastic box.

89
00:03:27,869 --> 00:03:29,689
A bright spot: most light.

90
00:03:31,397 --> 00:03:33,197
The cloudy plastic box.

91
00:03:33,777 --> 00:03:36,127
A soft glow: only some light.

92
00:03:37,035 --> 00:03:39,015
Both boxes are plastic!

93
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:45,320
Glass and some plastics are transparent.

94
00:03:45,590 --> 00:03:48,710
Frosted glass and some plastics are translucent.

95
00:03:50,295 --> 00:03:51,335
Two fingers?

96
00:03:51,575 --> 00:03:53,505
Put up two more on your score hand!

97
00:03:54,063 --> 00:03:55,168
Say it with us!

98
00:03:55,828 --> 00:03:56,884
Most light!

99
00:03:57,408 --> 00:03:58,502
Transparent!

100
00:04:02,228 --> 00:04:03,514
Only some light!

101
00:04:03,808 --> 00:04:04,990
Translucent!

102
00:04:08,628 --> 00:04:09,617
No light!

103
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:11,125
Opaque!

104
00:04:15,783 --> 00:04:17,253
Show me your score hand!

105
00:04:17,533 --> 00:04:18,583
More than one?

106
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:20,243
You beat the Buddies.

107
00:04:20,543 --> 00:04:21,603
Three fingers?

108
00:04:21,873 --> 00:04:22,883
High five!

109
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,828
Did you spot the moth?

110
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:26,768
It was by the corridor lamp!

111
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,368
Tell someone at home.

112
00:04:29,149 --> 00:04:31,649
Next time: a supermarket trolley!

113
00:04:31,939 --> 00:04:34,149
Which material would you choose to make it?

114
00:04:34,419 --> 00:04:35,489
One, glass.

115
00:04:35,759 --> 00:04:36,709
Two, metal.

116
00:04:37,009 --> 00:04:38,149
Three, fabric.

117
00:04:38,439 --> 00:04:39,759
Lock in your answer!

118
00:04:39,807 --> 00:04:41,007
A glass trolley!

119
00:04:41,057 --> 00:04:42,677
I could see all my snacks!

120
00:04:43,403 --> 00:04:45,603
Let's read today's key words together!

121
00:04:45,893 --> 00:04:46,653
Ready?

122
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:47,820
Opaque.

123
00:04:49,301 --> 00:04:50,298
Transparency.

124
00:04:52,164 --> 00:04:53,104
Well done!

125
00:04:54,086 --> 00:04:55,187
Say it with us!

126
00:04:55,987 --> 00:04:56,737
Ready?

127
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:57,520
One!

128
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:58,560
two!

129
00:04:58,865 --> 00:05:00,040
Now you know!
